kit: release-pipeline
version: 0.2.0
source: bamr87/bamr87 templates/release-pipeline/
seeded-by: tools/adopt-release.sh (adopts a repo; --upgrade refreshes an untouched release.yml)
files: ci.yml, release.yml, RELEASING.md
targets: ci.yml -> .github/workflows/ci.yml (only when the repo has no ci.yml); release.yml -> .github/workflows/release.yml; RELEASING.md -> RELEASING.md. release-please-config.json and .release-please-manifest.json are generated by the tool per ecosystem, not templated.
spec: specs/QUALITY.md UPS-QA-20/32/40, specs/WORK.md UPS-WORK-10, specs/REPOSITORY.md UPS-REPO-21
tests: tools/test_adopt_release.py (offline; stub gh, local clone)
updated: 2026-11-15
changelog: |
  0.2.0 — release.yml calls bamr87/.github's release-please.yml and
  publish.yml at @v1 instead of @main (UPS-WORK-10 and UPS-QA-40 reject a
  branch ref). The v1 tag holds both files byte-identical to main, with the
  same inputs, secrets and outputs, so a seeded repo releases exactly as
  before. The template carries a `# kit: release-pipeline vX.Y.Z` stamp, the
  kit gains this VERSION and archive/, and `tools/adopt-release.sh --upgrade`
  refreshes a release.yml that is byte-identical to the current template or to
  an archived shape. bamr87/bashos#97 hit the @main ref and was fixed by hand.
  0.1.0 — the kit as first shipped, unversioned (2026-06-17, #12): ci.yml,
  release.yml and RELEASING.md. Its release.yml is archive/release-0.1.0.yml.
notes: |
  - Placeholders: __DEFAULT_BRANCH__ and __KIT_VERSION__ in the workflows;
    __REGISTRY__, __VERSION_SOURCE__ and __SECRET__ in RELEASING.md.
  - Only release.yml is upgradeable. ci.yml is seeded only when a repo has no
    CI, and RELEASING.md and the release-please config are per-repo prose and
    data, so neither is ever overwritten.
  - Snapshot release.yml into archive/ BEFORE changing it (the rule every kit
    follows), with the stamp's version written out, as templates/verify/archive/
    does. Without the snapshot every deployed copy reads as hand-modified.
  - bamr87/.github's release-please.yml is the legacy caller under decision D3
    (UPS-REPO-21, warn-only while its rollout is `warn`); the sdlc kit seeds the
    hub's own release-please.yml@v2. Moving this kit there is a separate change.
